## 11. Onboarding Flow

## Step 1 — Welcome

**Your home, organized by AI.**
Know what you own, where it is, what it cost, and whether it's still covered.

Primary CTA: **Get Started** · Secondary: **Sign In**

---

## 12. Account Creation

Continue with Apple / Google / Email. Immediately after authentication, continue straight to the camera (§16) — no household, home, or profile configuration screens first.

---

## 13. Household & Home (auto-created)

A household and a default home are created invisibly at account creation, named from the account ("John's Home"), editable later from settings. No naming screen, no home-type/ownership/address form blocking onboarding. Address, if ever needed, is requested contextually (e.g., when a document requires it), never upfront.

---

## 14. Spaces (lightweight)

No pre-scan space checklist. The first time a user completes a scan, ask once, inline:

**Where was this?**

Freeform, autocomplete text field that creates a Space/Container as a side effect of naming it (typing "Garage" the first time creates the Garage space). Subsequent scans reuse and suggest existing spaces. This replaces the original 14-item space checklist entirely — it produced decision fatigue before any payoff and users rename rooms later anyway.

---

## 15. Product Goals (optional, lightweight)

Shown once, after the first successful scan, not before it — personalizes recommendations, never gates features.

**What would you like help managing?** *(multi-select, skippable)*

- Find & Organize Things
- Money & Spending
- Appliances & Warranties
- Home Maintenance
- Documents
- Home Map

*("Food & Meals" removed — see §6.)*

