## 16. First AI Experience

Immediately after account creation:

**Teach your home its first thing.**
Just take a photo. We'll figure out the rest.

Primary CTA: **Open Camera**

---

## 17. AI Scene Classification (launch scope: two types)

At launch, the camera supports two explicit modes rather than auto-detecting across everything:

- **Scan Item** — a bin, shelf, drawer, or collection of items
- **Scan Receipt** — a paper or digital receipt

A third explicit entry point, **Scan Appliance Label**, is available from the appliance flow (§28) but is not auto-classified at launch. Auto-classification across more types (§32) is added only as each underlying workflow proves reliable in production — not modeled speculatively up front.

---

## 18. Inventory Scan

User photographs a storage bin. AI detects: HDMI cable, USB-C charger, extension cord, batteries, power adapter.

**We found 5 items** — users can confirm, rename, remove, add a missing item, or change category.

Then: **Where is this?** (defaults from §14) and **Who does this belong to?** (defaults to Household).

CTA: **Add 5 Items**

---

## 19. AI Trust Requirement

AI-generated inventory must never become silently authoritative. Communicate uncertainty:

✓ USB-C Charger
? Electronic Adapter

Items below a confidence threshold are visibly flagged, not hidden.

---

## 20. First Success Experience

**Your home just got smarter.** 5 items added.

Then immediately demonstrate retrieval:

> Try asking: **Where are my AA batteries?**
> **AA Batteries** — Garage → Shelf → Bin 3

This teaches the core loop: **Scan → Understand → Find.** This is the moment onboarding is optimized to reach in under two minutes.

---

## 21. Main Home Dashboard

After first success, the user enters the normal app.

**Ask your home anything** — search/AI field
Quick actions: Scan · Find · Add
Summary: Items · Spaces · People

Additional modules appear based on §15 selections, but nothing is gated.

